## Output contract

Wrap your ENTIRE reply in a single ```yaml … ``` fence and nothing else — no
prose, no second fence, nothing before or after the fence.

The top level must have EXACTLY two keys: `format` and `sentences`. Do not add
any other top-level key. Each entry in `sentences` may use these keys only:

  - target        the {{script}} sentence (required)
  - romanisation  optional — include only if supplied or you derived it
  - english       optional — include only if supplied or you translated it
  - authority     optional map of field -> `human`, for learner-supplied fields only
  - tags          optional list of lowercase tags

Do NOT add literal glosses, word breakdowns, register, ids, audio, or source
metadata — those belong to the enrich stage.

## Example (shape only — do not copy these values)

```yaml
format: lingo.extract/v1
sentences:
  - target: "अध्यापक जी, यहाँ कितने विद्यार्थी हैं?"
    romanisation: "adhyāpak jī, yahā̃ kitne vidyārthī haĩ?"
    english: "Teacher ji, how many students are here?"
    authority:
      english: human
    tags:
      - classroom
      - question
  - target: "मैं ठीक हूँ।"
    romanisation: "maĩ ṭhīk hū̃."
    english: "I am fine."
```

The raw text follows.
